From your screenshot, you're editing the autoscaling section:

YAML
autoscaling:
enabled: false
minReplicas: 5
maxReplicas: 100
 

⚠️ minReplicas and maxReplicas will not change the current pod count because:

YAML
enabled: false
 

means HPA (Horizontal Pod Autoscaler) is disabled.

To change pod count manually

Find the top of values.yaml and change:

YAML
replicaCount: 1

to:

YAML
replicaCount: 5
 

Save the file.

Then run:

Shell
helm upgrade myapp ./myapp

Verify:

Shell
kubectl get pods

Expected:

Plain Text
myapp-xxxxx 1/1 Running
myapp-yyyyy 1/1 Running
myapp-zzzzz 1/1 Running
myapp-aaaaa 1/1 Running
myapp-bbbbb 1/1 Running
Check whether deployment uses replicaCount
Shell
grep replicas templates/deployment.yaml

You should see:

YAML
replicas: {{ .Values.replicaCount }}

If not, open:

Shell
nano templates/deployment.yaml

and make sure it contains:

YAML
spec:
replicas: {{ .Values.replicaCount }}

Then:

Shell
helm upgrade myapp ./myapp
Verify deployment size
Shell
kubectl get deployment myapp

Output should be similar to:

Plain Text
NAME READY UP-TO-DATE AVAILABLE
myapp 5/5 5 5

You can also directly set 5 replicas without editing the file:

Shell
helm upgrade myapp ./myapp --set replicaCount=5

This is the quickest Helm command to increase pods from 1 → 5.

